tuxamp (0.1.6~alpha) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fixed: while casting, moving an EQ band slider or picking a preset
    paused the music, because the whole stream was re-sent to the device.
    The stream is now sent at playback pace, about 3 s ahead of the
    device, with the EQ applied as it is sent, so changes fade in on the
    device with no pause, no buffering and no restart.
  * Fixed: EQ and balance changes reaching a cast device are cross-faded,
    so they never click.
  * Documents updated (README, BUGFIXES.md).

 -- Shawn Rapaz <shawnrapaz@gmail.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:09:50 +0900

tuxamp (0.1.5~alpha) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fixed: the preamp was not real time. The sound now follows the preamp
    and EQ sliders while they are dragged (about 0.1 s behind, was about
    0.2 s), and nothing pauses on release.
  * Fixed: the preamp did nothing while the EQ was off; grabbing a slider
    now switches the EQ on.
  * Fixed: a rare skipped piece of audio (a click) while the EQ changed.
  * Casting: the preamp now changes the device's volume instantly instead
    of re-sending the stream (which paused it) when the slider was let go.
  * Documents updated (README, BUGFIXES.md).

 -- Shawn Rapaz <shawnrapaz@gmail.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:38:21 +0900

tuxamp (0.1.4~alpha) unstable; urgency=medium

